{"kind":"assert","text":"A fact for the ruling on c479fcec. The store-format race comes from the cutover branch, not from main or NF-3.\n\n- Commit 28ca945c \"Refuse old local store formats before reading their records\" (12 Nov) adds `packages/mcp/src/store-format.ts` on the cutover branch. It is not an ancestor of main 64112e45.\n- Main 64112e45 has no `store-format.ts` in any package. NF-3 moved the custody file store to `packages/client/src/node.ts` and added no format word.\n- The merge 055aa081 (cutover c38bf62a plus main 64112e45) moves the file to `packages/client/src/store-format.ts`.\n\nThe `openSync(path, \"wx\")` create and the rule \"A partial or incompatible word refuses; no retry or repair follows\" (`store-format.ts:48-51` at 28ca945c) are therefore new in the cutover head. The reason c479fcec gives for option (a), that the code is main's and the cutover does not change it, does not hold. At the cutover review I will treat the race as part of that head: two processes that open one new store can refuse it as retired.","body":{"to":"planner"}}